## 4.3 Fact-Level Indexing System

Every individual factual statement must receive a unique, deterministic fact_id.

Examples:

EXP-1-B1
EXP-1-B2
EXP-2-B1

PRJ-1-B1
PRJ-2-B1

EDU-1-F1
EDU-1-F2

SKL-01
SKL-02
SKL-03

HDR-01
HDR-02

Rules:

- IDs must be generated by application code, not Gemini.
- IDs must remain stable when facts are edited.
- IDs must not change when facts are reordered.
- Deleted IDs must not be silently reassigned to different facts.
- Newly added facts receive new IDs.
- Every bullet point must have its own ID.
- Every independently usable skill must have its own ID.
- Every role, qualification, achievement, and relevant structured field must be individually traceable.

Use a centralized fact ID generator.

Store facts as structured records rather than plain strings.

Suggested fact structure:

{
  "fact_id": "EXP-1-B1",
  "section": "experience",
  "parent_id": "EXP-1",
  "content": "Developed REST APIs using Python and FastAPI.",
  "approved": true,
  "created_at": "...",
  "updated_at": "...",
  "source": "user_supplied_resume"
}

Use appropriate additional metadata when needed.

