# PART 15 — TESTING AND ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

Do not consider the application complete until the following workflows have been tested.

### Test 1 — Sample Profile

- Load Sample CS Graduate Profile.
- Verify all five profile sections.
- Verify deterministic fact IDs.
- Approve sample facts.
- Refresh the page.
- Confirm persistence.

### Test 2 — PDF Extraction

- Upload a PDF resume.
- Confirm browser-native base64 conversion.
- Confirm Gemini receives inlineData.
- Confirm structured extraction.
- Confirm facts are initially pending approval.
- Approve selected facts.

### Test 3 — Fact Approval

- Add a new fact.
- Edit an existing fact.
- Confirm edited facts require reapproval.
- Delete a fact.
- Confirm deleted IDs are not reused.
- Confirm rejected facts are excluded.

### Test 4 — Tailoring

- Enter a realistic software engineering job description.
- Add a focus directive.
- Generate a resume.
- Confirm all generated bullets contain valid source fact IDs.
- Confirm unsupported profile requirements appear as missing.

### Test 5 — Independent Audit

- Confirm Pass 2 executes separately from Pass 1.
- Confirm every bullet receives an audit result.
- Confirm invalid source references are flagged.
- Confirm unsupported claims cannot be silently exported.

### Test 6 — Manual Editing

- Edit a generated bullet.
- Confirm its previous verification status is invalidated.
- Re-run the audit.
- Confirm the new result is displayed.

### Test 7 — Export

- Export PDF.
- Confirm only the clean resume is printed.
- Export Word.
- Confirm the downloaded document opens as a readable Word-compatible document.
- Copy plain text.
- Confirm the clipboard contains only the resume content.

### Test 8 — Version History

- Generate two resumes.
- Confirm both versions are saved.
- Reopen the first version.
- Confirm the exact original snapshot appears.
- Duplicate a version.
- Delete a version.
- Refresh the browser.
- Confirm persistence.

### Test 9 — Error Recovery

- Simulate an AI failure.
- Confirm existing resume content is preserved.
- Simulate malformed localStorage data.
- Confirm the application recovers without crashing.

### Test 10 — Responsive UI

- Test desktop.
- Test tablet.
- Test mobile.
- Confirm no broken layouts or inaccessible controls.

